  <static seed="1773" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/Decimal/AddSubtractDecimals20.pg">
    <statement><p>Simplify without using a calculator.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 6.7 - 5.88 }</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.82</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To subtract two decimals, make sure to line up the decimal points:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \amp \phantom{-}6.70 \\
 \amp \underline{-5.88\phantom{ad}} \\
   \amp \phantom{-}0.82
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Note that we added an extra <m>0</m> to the end of <m>6.7</m> before doing subtraction.</p>
</solution>
